distribution: check_mk
description:
 Info of a MikroTik RouterOS Board

 This check reports model, RouterOS version, serial number and
 RouterBOOT firmware of a MikroTik RouterOS device.

 If a minimum RouterOS version is defined, the check goes {WARN}
 if the installed version is below it.

 If /system/routerboard reports an upgrade-firmware higher than
 current-firmware, a RouterBOOT firmware upgrade is pending
 (/system/routerboard upgrade, then reboot). The check goes {WARN}
 by default; the state is configurable.

 Serial number and firmware need agent version 4.1.0 or later and
 are only reported by devices that have a RouterBOARD.

 The same data is written to the HW/SW inventory (hardware.system,
 software.os, software.firmware) if the "Do HW/SW Inventory" rule
 applies to the host.

 To connect to the MikroTik device a special datasource program is
 used (SNMP won't report this information): {MikroTik RouterOS} in
 Setup > Agents> Other integrations > Hardware

